{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:29:16.633486Z","id":"03844519752781210163b9d3bfaa40e0b157ff5f521343142a570d585bca8e4d","body":{"detail":"Tick::turn races the stream against the cancel token; on cancel it commits a stopped step with no token usage, because the assembled message (and its usage) never arrives. The provider charges the instance key for input already processed and output already streamed. Spec section 7.3 says a failed model call charges nothing, so this follows the spec, but it is a margin leak a person could repeat (send, cancel, send). Tracking the last MessageDelta usage seen through the delta callback would give a lower bound to charge.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1298},"end":{"line":1311},"content_hash":"c22c70e96fdcb0e01c87761df61482774ee5297c17402bb39349177c599b598b"},"summary":"A turn cancelled mid-stream charges no tokens, though the provider billed what it streamed","tags":["credits","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:29:16.633646Z","id":"c228e4eb6c2742f2c0baa39fddf23bf84037749f576cab0e98b51335e81f1681","body":{"detail":"On a retryable model error the turn sleeps RetryPolicy::delay (up to its cap, 8 s by default) with clax_rt::time::sleep outside `watched`, so a cancel waits for the sleep to end and the lease is not renewed during it (the cap is far below the 60 s lease, so this is latency, not a lost claim).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1312},"end":{"line":1327},"content_hash":"962c6f33aa473396f9533040d3d7e7470fc6750a3bee4b81acd0d271d06b9976"},"summary":"A retry wait inside a turn does not watch the cancel token or renew the lease","tags":["cancel","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:29:16.633706Z","id":"5f249ff529a1d743da4f759651ce54db02eee7d61a0dad99776db78b63e71aa4","body":{"detail":"OpCtx::key is <run>:<step>:<seq>, seq the call's place among the step's host calls. A step executed again after a crash reuses the keys, so a BotHost answers a repeated write with its first answer. If the re-run script takes another path (a read now returns other data, so it makes a different call at the same seq), a key can name a different write: the host would answer it with the earlier, unrelated answer. A BotHost should refuse (or log) a key reused for a different op or arguments; FakeBotHost (host.rs) does not check.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":48},"content_hash":"bb27f2a1bdc98abf1fa66209ea43d313d3e8792f33ec4a189e3499519ffd605b"},"summary":"Exactly-once host writes rest on a re-executed script making the same calls in the same order","tags":["idempotency","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:29:16.633794Z","id":"2cabfead2a12668d65024410555b3c2dcae7518d844af8256ba618b42a7addc2","body":{"detail":"draft.publish sends if_version = the draft's base (the run's base_version, or the version the run last published). When someone else published meanwhile the host answers conflict and the model sees it, but no operation re-bases the draft on the new version, so every retry conflicts again until the run gives up. Spec section 6.3 says the model may re-read and retry; that needs a draft.rebase (or files.* reading through to the latest version) in the API.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1662},"end":{"line":1700},"content_hash":"c284a46c2474da37e5118965eaabc99c11250b3e2c806b16601efa93dde40bb1"},"summary":"A publish conflict cannot be recovered by the model: the draft has no rebase","tags":["gap","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:29:16.633878Z","id":"c4f58f3d0efa9801fb4aa39ca74a690b72ecdbabcd167f8c0c0e97095fed4d49","body":{"detail":"With infra_lines on (the Worker), each step charges do.requests = 1 + its host calls and toolpath.storage = the payload's JSON bytes for 30 days. Neither is read from Cloudflare's billing: spec section 13 lists this as a known gap. The payload holds the script's code and outcome, so storage scales with output, not with what the journal keeps.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":734},"end":{"line":751},"content_hash":"a285f354d4d0ba6d866272581bd830661fecdf93fd6dc566656d2ede7475903f"},"summary":"Durable Object requests and Toolpath storage are estimated per step","tags":["credits","gap","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:29:16.633946Z","id":"d87dc7c55df3512115b711439b9bcdaf1c9f34d221ee27e0b26b1257fac57e3a","body":{"detail":"tick reads run_with_steps and History::of parses each payload (assistant blocks, script code and outcome, the first turn's system prompt) to rebuild the messages, so a run of N steps does O(N) work and reads O(total payload) per tick, O(N^2) over the run. Bounded by max_steps (40 by default); a cache of the history keyed by the last committed step would make it O(1).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":504},"end":{"line":512},"content_hash":"99ad874535515538a331aec47318e2de4a28687146eede1e55e8bba0a55c2538"},"summary":"Every tick rebuilds the whole history from every committed step's payload","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/check.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:29:16.634003Z","id":"f787010f66400ea59d8162ad01b36cfebaea04bf81422d9de5a236942ce1a893","body":{"detail":"contract_problems finds :root tokens, the two dark-mode blocks and a body background by scanning rule selectors and bodies between braces (comments stripped). Nested at-rules other than @media, selectors spread oddly or tokens set from script can give a false problem or miss one. A CSS parser (lightningcss, cssparser) was not taken to keep the crate light on wasm32.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":201},"end":{"line":230},"content_hash":"127a42bf9c1e5da88e112b76ee06563599b5e14bb310c31b4820d555ba776895"},"summary":"The page-contract lint reads CSS textually, not with a CSS parser","tags":["revisit:draft.check reports false contract problems on real pages","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/events.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:29:16.634070Z","id":"7594c66c5c810f3ae0d2d6d0401461b449e7cc7e37ea90912783f322178d09da","body":{"detail":"Live step_done events carry the step's charge from Store::commit_step; the canonical events rebuilt from committed steps read payload.credits_milli, which the payload never has (the charge is computed at commit), so a client that reconnects sees credits only in run_credits_milli. The store could return the step's charge with the steps (a sum of its usage rows) for the replay.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":338},"end":{"line":346},"content_hash":"2b2bfd0310632ca4d73355069aed67d441fa2660e9d19a83573da3d2c35cf913"},"summary":"A replayed step_done carries no credits for its step","tags":["events","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T02:29:16.634133Z","id":"d7b66d99de5d1d42cc3e7b2c9a093a86efee637b3509ef7b0dc82dc894a0b089","body":{"detail":"Spec section 8: locally a value in config.toml or the environment overrides the stored one. from_store reads Store::bot_setting and leaves per_person_concurrency, lease and renewal at their defaults; the daemon's SettingsSource must apply HomeConfig::bot (including bot.per_person_concurrency and enabled) on top, re-read per tick.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":138},"end":{"line":142},"content_hash":"26d90fcdfbcd7a1130c94a90470682b5ff5383da70d7c0c4dc1fe2dfb535d677"},"summary":"RunSettings::from_store reads the database only: the [bot] config overrides are the server's to lay over it","tags":["wiring","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:53:22.718136Z","id":"6e12d44d65db97b30a223291348fd83781a29f1734040b8884155c59307333e9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a83e61a3","summary":"Fixed: a turn's usage is recorded on its open step as it streams (Store::observe_step) and a cancelled call is charged to the person at the stopped step's commit (crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs Observed::charge). Evidence: //crates/clax-bot:integration cancel::a_cancel_mid_turn_stops_the_run_and_charges_what_the_call_used passes (ledger tokens equal what the fake provider served).","supersedes":"03844519752781210163b9d3bfaa40e0b157ff5f521343142a570d585bca8e4d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:53:22.738752Z","id":"c33eee6dc2b96728bd8c560203ce41f4e839684ce39e21084dfd422d2dd91e15","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a83e61a3","summary":"Fixed: the retry wait runs inside `watched` (lease renewed, store cancel seen) and races the cancel token, and a retry starts only with min_turn_budget left (crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs Tick::turn). Evidence: //crates/clax-bot:integration money::a_cut_stream_retried_in_the_tick_is_absorbed_and_the_retry_charged passes.","supersedes":"c228e4eb6c2742f2c0baa39fddf23bf84037749f576cab0e98b51335e81f1681","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:53:22.757919Z","id":"bbaa924bf1cea8922f16266f1ea4b298886819f06675b98b84364e4e965692b5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a83e61a3","summary":"Fixed: every script call is journaled per step (bot_calls) and a step run again is answered from the journal, ending with replay_diverged when a call differs (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs); host writes are journaled in their own transaction through JournalSlot/Journaled, which refuse a key reused for other arguments. Evidence: //crates/clax-bot:integration rules::a_script_run_again_that_takes_another_path_stops_where_it_diverged, rules::the_fake_host_passes_the_host_conformance_suite and resume::* pass.","supersedes":"5f249ff529a1d743da4f759651ce54db02eee7d61a0dad99776db78b63e71aa4","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:53:22.777665Z","id":"20fdb9fa92c3db5b3742650a60a6c288efc38a839b82c123c309e33759138a32","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:a83e61a3","summary":"Fixed: draft.rebase() moves the draft onto the current version keeping its changes and reports conflicts, and draft.theirs(path) reads the other side (crates/clax-bot/src/draft.rs Draft::rebase). Evidence: //crates/clax-bot:integration rules::a_draft_is_rebased_over_a_version_someone_else_published passes.","supersedes":"2cabfead2a12668d65024410555b3c2dcae7518d844af8256ba618b42a7addc2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:53:22.797364Z","id":"2f8fe43884439c9cdf088a0b2833daf86063a175ea849b59028bdd54b2d0f121","body":{"detail":"Spec section 8: locally a value in config.toml or the environment overrides the stored one. from_store reads Store::bot_setting and leaves per_person_concurrency, lease and renewal at their defaults; the daemon's SettingsSource must apply HomeConfig::bot (including bot.per_person_concurrency and enabled) on top, re-read per tick.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":146},"end":{"line":150},"content_hash":"26d90fcdfbcd7a1130c94a90470682b5ff5383da70d7c0c4dc1fe2dfb535d677"},"summary":"RunSettings::from_store reads the database only: the [bot] config overrides are the server's to lay over it","supersedes":"d7b66d99de5d1d42cc3e7b2c9a093a86efee637b3509ef7b0dc82dc894a0b089","tags":["wiring","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:53:22.817260Z","id":"981099eb68e70f6f24fece32bafebcae46270018b4cd1d3fd5cec23bfb03d718","body":{"detail":"tick reads run_with_steps and History::of parses each payload (assistant blocks, script code and outcome, the first turn's system prompt) to rebuild the messages, so a run of N steps does O(N) work and reads O(total payload) per tick, O(N^2) over the run. Bounded by max_steps (40 by default); a cache of the history keyed by the last committed step would make it O(1).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":534},"end":{"line":542},"content_hash":"1e7c494d01b9bd2670be02ff48ec4d5300171eb6e49f41c1f8ce2087181447ff"},"summary":"Every tick rebuilds the whole history from every committed step's payload","supersedes":"d87dc7c55df3512115b711439b9bcdaf1c9f34d221ee27e0b26b1257fac57e3a","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:53:22.836815Z","id":"7cf431f38b261e332dd1766c94af9c72afb6eeca310a34f4b58d5a14cde9d5ad","body":{"detail":"With infra_lines on (the Worker), each step charges do.requests = 1 + its host calls and toolpath.storage = the payload's JSON bytes for 30 days. Neither is read from Cloudflare's billing: spec section 13 lists this as a known gap. The payload holds the script's code and outcome, so storage scales with output, not with what the journal keeps.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":806},"end":{"line":823},"content_hash":"f8cbfeb27151f233944bd59251c9474323c8129dec57467d03bdad986c1589f3"},"summary":"Durable Object requests and Toolpath storage are estimated per step","supersedes":"c4f58f3d0efa9801fb4aa39ca74a690b72ecdbabcd167f8c0c0e97095fed4d49","tags":["credits","gap","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/events.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:53:22.858008Z","id":"b31ddcab70856e03c45a23685389874c5e7d4a5e4103a27abd7d20451e7e8c48","body":{"detail":"Live step_done events carry the step's charge from Store::commit_step; the canonical events rebuilt from committed steps read payload.credits_milli, which the payload never has (the charge is computed at commit), so a client that reconnects sees credits only in run_credits_milli. The store could return the step's charge with the steps (a sum of its usage rows) for the replay.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":350},"end":{"line":358},"content_hash":"6ef3cc4175985ad706c0e6a44514f28225e8ecc43f5d42817c1458c0476a6025"},"summary":"A replayed step_done carries no credits for its step","supersedes":"7594c66c5c810f3ae0d2d6d0401461b449e7cc7e37ea90912783f322178d09da","tags":["events","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:53:22.917504Z","id":"65a5e58c3991f60d84c994b4338dd69721e5ac7f69a93e4aff99fc908fdd5250","body":{"detail":"Tick::affordable prices the request as its JSON bytes / 4 tokens, the part the last turn cached at the cached-input rate and the rest at the input rate, then caps max_tokens to the output the credits left pay for. A request whose tokens run well above bytes/4 (non-Latin text, dense JSON) can still overshoot the person's credits by its input; counting tokens (the Messages API count_tokens endpoint) would bound it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1403},"end":{"line":1465},"content_hash":"3781cdb210a7ba32e5a8ac60c65d9dfe4dacfc04a1dde81315f0c11e3f1c2faa"},"summary":"A turn's affordable max_tokens rests on a byte-count estimate of its input","tags":["credits","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T03:53:22.917555Z","id":"fc4c1eae84db277bf4a1cc7cf8b936bfb61303605497dd0efd4d2b4d4b3c699d","body":{"detail":"JournalSlot::record_with runs the write in the store transaction that journals it, which needs a write path that accepts a transaction. A route code path that commits on its own (an async publish whose content is written before its version row) has to call JournalSlot::record_in on its final transaction; calling record_with around it would journal in a second transaction, and a crash between the two would let a resumed step write again. FakeBotHost::publish (crates/clax-bot/src/host.rs) checks the journal before publishing and journals after, which has that gap.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":125},"end":{"line":207},"content_hash":"806748e955b729403c61d9754ea39c2f35b0ffb85dbbde8eab1701797bbba41a"},"summary":"A host write path that opens its own transaction must journal with record_in inside it, or the write and its entry are not atomic","tags":["idempotency","wiring","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:14:44.514194Z","id":"67173b9e0070fdf0ed96b5bceb501bc578adb6fb67b14bf8b1a8c571b006ef9a","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"2f8fe43884439c9cdf088a0b2833daf86063a175ea849b59028bdd54b2d0f121","summary":"The server now lays [bot] over the database inside the store (Store::set_bot_overrides, crates/clax-store/src/bot_settings.rs, set by clax_server::serve's local_bot from the configuration in effect), so RunSettings::from_store and the credit arithmetic read the overrides on every read (bot_settings::tests::overrides_win_on_every_read_and_refuse_writes). Proposed close: fixed in git:bf3458ec.","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T07:11:08.903848Z","id":"7110883538641a4e864f485a2a9f6d166bf04b1082080ac7512a5cb552fa2e35","body":{"detail":"With infra_lines on (the Worker), each step charges do.requests = 1 + its host calls and toolpath.storage = the payload's JSON bytes for 30 days. Neither is read from Cloudflare's billing: spec section 13 lists this as a known gap. The payload holds the script's code and outcome, so storage scales with output, not with what the journal keeps.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":840},"end":{"line":857},"content_hash":"f8cbfeb27151f233944bd59251c9474323c8129dec57467d03bdad986c1589f3"},"summary":"Durable Object requests and Toolpath storage are estimated per step","supersedes":"7cf431f38b261e332dd1766c94af9c72afb6eeca310a34f4b58d5a14cde9d5ad","tags":["credits","gap","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T07:11:08.923470Z","id":"1c94e938e8275d9cbe416565e699413131e294e130f97f3d6f5b5ba3121d07bd","body":{"detail":"Tick::affordable prices the request as its JSON bytes / 4 tokens, the part the last turn cached at the cached-input rate and the rest at the input rate, then caps max_tokens to the output the credits left pay for. A request whose tokens run well above bytes/4 (non-Latin text, dense JSON) can still overshoot the person's credits by its input; counting tokens (the Messages API count_tokens endpoint) would bound it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1455},"end":{"line":1517},"content_hash":"3781cdb210a7ba32e5a8ac60c65d9dfe4dacfc04a1dde81315f0c11e3f1c2faa"},"summary":"A turn's affordable max_tokens rests on a byte-count estimate of its input","supersedes":"65a5e58c3991f60d84c994b4338dd69721e5ac7f69a93e4aff99fc908fdd5250","tags":["credits","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T07:11:09.225899Z","id":"602c5cdd938f4e15a10aff1fdc8d2bd36e41299ba9e8ec3c2def076be01100e2","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:8c175a71","summary":"Fixed structurally: a BotHost no longer performs writes; it answers a WritePlan that the run loop runs with the journal entry, and a plan can only answer with a clax_store::Journaled, which only the store's journaled write paths make, each recording the entry in the write's own transaction (e8694915). Evidence: //crates/clax-bot:integration rules::the_fake_host_passes_the_host_conformance_suite passes, including a_crash_between_a_write_and_its_journal_entry_writes_once (Store::set_journal_fault fails the write after it and before its entry; the resumed write makes one reply); //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test bot_runs::tests::a_journaled_comment_and_its_entry_commit_together_or_not_at_all passes.","supersedes":"fc4c1eae84db277bf4a1cc7cf8b936bfb61303605497dd0efd4d2b4d4b3c699d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T07:11:09.245621Z","id":"8ace4b233429a403eb3ec6fa49bf4f8bbbeb7948dbe52bb5d82638ee7d52e7e9","body":{"detail":"plan_reply and plan_write(threads.reply): Store::add_comment_journaled(ctx, thread_id, NewComment{author_kind: AUTHOR_AGENT, author_name: \"ClaxBot\", ..}, &entry), value {comment_id}. plan_write(threads.resolve): Store::resolve_thread_journaled(ctx, thread_id, by, Some(person), &entry). plan_write(db.set|db.update|db.delete): Store::doc_set_journaled / doc_update_journaled / doc_delete_journaled(ctx, artifact, path, .., pin, caller, &entry), value {id, version} or null. plan_publish: Store::publish_version_journaled(ctx, artifact, validated, session, &entry).await, value {version}. artifacts.create (a brief run, once): no journaled path exists yet; add one (create_artifact with the entry recorded in its transaction) or build it on Store::with_bot_journal(&entry, |tx| ..) once creation has a Tx variant. Checks (rights, the run's threads, the artifact) go in plan_*, before the plan is returned; a plan must not write any other way. Pass host_conformance::check_host with a fixture over real threads.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":265},"end":{"line":302},"content_hash":"7958ccd5fcfa2c285137b9da2144537a3688ddcaa959c1315954dfd68eb5cf60"},"summary":"For the server's BotHost: build every write plan over the store's journaled write paths, passing the plan's CallEntry","tags":["wiring","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:18:57.870906Z","id":"f8861165df8a28ed570b5ecabfd162be3dc9ed3d9e53b54fd8284ba8d85c8a55","body":{"detail":"Every write has a journaled path; none other may be used. plan_reply and plan_write(threads.reply): Store::add_comment_journaled(ctx, thread_id, NewComment{author_kind: AUTHOR_AGENT, author_name: \"ClaxBot\", ..}, &entry, guard), value {comment_id}. threads.resolve: Store::resolve_thread_journaled(ctx, thread_id, by, Some(person), &entry, guard). db.set|db.update|db.delete: Store::doc_set_journaled / doc_update_journaled / doc_delete_journaled(ctx, artifact, \"<collection>/<id>\", .., pin, caller, &entry, guard), value {id, version} or null. draft.publish: Store::publish_version_journaled(ctx, artifact, validated, session, &entry, guard).await, value {version}. artifacts.create (a brief run, once): Store::create_artifact_journaled(ctx, validated, session, &entry, guard).await, value {id}. Anything else: Store::with_bot_journal(&entry, guard, |tx| ..). The CallEntry comes from the run loop (Store::call_entry, for the driver holding the run); a plan cannot make one. The guard (clax_store::Guard) runs inside the write's transaction: it must re-check that the acting person may still write on the artifact (their share, membership, the claxbot flag), so a revoke between plan and run writes nothing. Checks that need no transaction (the run's threads, the artifact, the op) go in plan_*. Pass host_conformance::check_host with a fixture over real threads, including its revoke callback.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":255},"end":{"line":292},"content_hash":"7958ccd5fcfa2c285137b9da2144537a3688ddcaa959c1315954dfd68eb5cf60"},"summary":"For the server's BotHost: build every write plan over the store's journaled write paths, passing the plan's CallEntry and a guard","supersedes":"8ace4b233429a403eb3ec6fa49bf4f8bbbeb7948dbe52bb5d82638ee7d52e7e9","tags":["wiring","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:18:57.890510Z","id":"e0763849212b77b9e65e376c99f7058d51e04d68b364360ee30b78dacf58b5bd","body":{"detail":"Tick::affordable prices the request as its JSON bytes / 4 tokens, the part the last turn cached at the cached-input rate and the rest at the input rate, then caps max_tokens to the output the credits left pay for. A request whose tokens run well above bytes/4 (non-Latin text, dense JSON) can still overshoot the person's credits by its input; counting tokens (the Messages API count_tokens endpoint) would bound it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1480},"end":{"line":1542},"content_hash":"3781cdb210a7ba32e5a8ac60c65d9dfe4dacfc04a1dde81315f0c11e3f1c2faa"},"summary":"A turn's affordable max_tokens rests on a byte-count estimate of its input","supersedes":"1c94e938e8275d9cbe416565e699413131e294e130f97f3d6f5b5ba3121d07bd","tags":["credits","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/host.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T12:35:22.188073Z","id":"ce0151cf701ec4d82b3c4cf7d6078ce5af4fc3c2c0f7a6e632a756591be489fd","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"f8861165df8a28ed570b5ecabfd162be3dc9ed3d9e53b54fd8284ba8d85c8a55","summary":"Done in clax_server::bot::ServerHost (git:0c8d388e): each plan writes only through the journaled path the record names, with a guard (Store::check_bot_write_in, crates/clax-store/src/people.rs) that re-reads inside the write's transaction whether the run's person is still connected, still has the claxbot flag and still holds the right (comments write; artifacts update for documents and publishes; artifacts create for artifacts.create). Evidence: bazelisk test //crates/clax-server:integration__3 --test_arg=api_claxbot_run:: passes the_servers_host_passes_the_bot_host_conformance_suite (every case, crash and revoke included) and a_run_edits_publishes_and_replies_as_claxbot_for_its_person. Proposed close.","tags":["session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:57:56.645957Z","id":"f8455fc2bcb9723fab12134c95a00dc92e9ceb4ccced73ff8dc67153c8a7621f","body":{"detail":"tick reads run_with_steps and History::of parses each payload (assistant blocks, script code and outcome, the first turn's system prompt) to rebuild the messages, so a run of N steps does O(N) work and reads O(total payload) per tick, O(N^2) over the run. Bounded by max_steps (40 by default); a cache of the history keyed by the last committed step would make it O(1).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":552},"end":{"line":560},"content_hash":"1e7c494d01b9bd2670be02ff48ec4d5300171eb6e49f41c1f8ce2087181447ff"},"summary":"Every tick rebuilds the whole history from every committed step's payload","supersedes":"981099eb68e70f6f24fece32bafebcae46270018b4cd1d3fd5cec23bfb03d718","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:57:56.696018Z","id":"005784c51df83b1cb74ac0c31dcfe53953f95413f0255bb16f370221b5cf3e81","body":{"detail":"With infra_lines on (the Worker), each step charges do.requests = 1 + its host calls and toolpath.storage = the payload's JSON bytes for 30 days. Neither is read from Cloudflare's billing: spec section 13 lists this as a known gap. The payload holds the script's code and outcome, so storage scales with output, not with what the journal keeps.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":858},"end":{"line":875},"content_hash":"f8cbfeb27151f233944bd59251c9474323c8129dec57467d03bdad986c1589f3"},"summary":"Durable Object requests and Toolpath storage are estimated per step","supersedes":"7110883538641a4e864f485a2a9f6d166bf04b1082080ac7512a5cb552fa2e35","tags":["credits","gap","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T14:57:56.765212Z","id":"57474f0d125482861643254910e9ac91e7236ed08f7305dae0f7507ff6b47c8e","body":{"detail":"Tick::affordable prices the request as its JSON bytes / 4 tokens, the part the last turn cached at the cached-input rate and the rest at the input rate, then caps max_tokens to the output the credits left pay for. A request whose tokens run well above bytes/4 (non-Latin text, dense JSON) can still overshoot the person's credits by its input; counting tokens (the Messages API count_tokens endpoint) would bound it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1504},"end":{"line":1566},"content_hash":"3781cdb210a7ba32e5a8ac60c65d9dfe4dacfc04a1dde81315f0c11e3f1c2faa"},"summary":"A turn's affordable max_tokens rests on a byte-count estimate of its input","supersedes":"e0763849212b77b9e65e376c99f7058d51e04d68b364360ee30b78dacf58b5bd","tags":["credits","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:43:26.199137Z","id":"94a4332dfadbffa08734d4af6baa02ff2581fe215614029decbb419df7b45503","body":{"detail":"tick reads run_with_steps and History::of parses each payload (assistant blocks, script code and outcome, the first turn's system prompt) to rebuild the messages, so a run of N steps does O(N) work and reads O(total payload) per tick, O(N^2) over the run. Bounded by max_steps (40 by default); a cache of the history keyed by the last committed step would make it O(1).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":556},"end":{"line":564},"content_hash":"1e7c494d01b9bd2670be02ff48ec4d5300171eb6e49f41c1f8ce2087181447ff"},"summary":"Every tick rebuilds the whole history from every committed step's payload","supersedes":"f8455fc2bcb9723fab12134c95a00dc92e9ceb4ccced73ff8dc67153c8a7621f","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/run.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T15:43:26.221593Z","id":"6f3e5c2c3e1dbfee419a8ff9816ba4506a9f168fe09e9c4df6a4b8803d9bb766","body":{"detail":"With infra_lines on (the Worker), each step charges do.requests = 1 + its host calls and toolpath.storage = the payload's JSON bytes for 30 days. Neither is read from Cloudflare's billing: spec section 13 lists this as a known gap. The payload holds the script's code and outcome, so storage scales with output, not with what the journal keeps.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":862},"end":{"line":879},"content_hash":"f8cbfeb27151f233944bd59251c9474323c8129dec57467d03bdad986c1589f3"},"summary":"Durable Object requests and Toolpath storage are estimated per step","supersedes":"005784c51df83b1cb74ac0c31dcfe53953f95413f0255bb16f370221b5cf3e81","tags":["credits","gap","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
